      <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/77f48231-7e0c-4918-a92a-48bd602a2a58,1765687617803/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C166%2C6885%2C3872%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Hockey players celebrate on the ice.' width='620' height='349' title='United States players celebrates a goal as Canada's Sarah Fillier (10) skates past during second period Rivalry Series action in Edmonton on Saturday, December 13, 2025. THE CANADIAN PRESS/Jason Franson'/><p>Hilary Knight scored twice, including an empty-netter, to lead the United States to a 4-1 win over Canada in a women's hockey Rivalry Series game Saturday.</p>]]></description>
